<p>We do not use your data for fully automated decisions that have legal or similarly significant effects on you.</p>

<h2 id="pupil-data">4. Pupil data: what we process on a school's behalf</h2>

<p>A school or instructor can record, for each pupil: name, contact details, date of birth, address and pickup addresses, driving licence number and expiry, theory-test details, lesson history and outcomes, progress against the DVSA skills, notes, payment and balance records, messages, and uploaded documents. They can also record an emergency contact and a parent's details.</p>

<p>A school can choose to record <strong>health information</strong> (a medical notes field, and uploaded medical certificates) and <strong>ID documents</strong>. Health information is special category data. The school needs a condition under UK GDPR Article 9 for it (for example, to make a reasonable adjustment for a pupil with a disability) and should record only what it needs. Our terms ask schools to keep health details out of free-text lesson notes.</p>

<p>We act only on the school's instructions. Our <a href="/data-processing-terms/">Data Processing Terms</a> set out the rules and the security measures.</p>

<h2 id="pupils-under-18">5. Pupils under 18</h2>

<p>Pupils aged 16 and 17 learn to drive and use the pupil app and portal. Some pupils may be 17 or younger when a parent books for them.</p>

<ul>
<li>Your school (not us) decides what is recorded about you and relies on its own lawful basis. For a driving lesson booking that is usually contract (you have asked for lessons) or legitimate interests.</li>
<li>We do not use pupil data for advertising and we do not profile pupils for marketing.</li>
<li>Our product analytics and screen recordings (PostHog) never run on pupil or parent pages. If Google Analytics is switched on in the app, it loads on every page of the app, including pupil and parent pages, but only after the person using it clicks "Accept All" in the app's cookie banner. Choosing "Necessary Only" stops it.</li>
<li>We want the notice to be understandable by someone aged 16. If any part is not, tell us at <a href="mailto:privacy@driveschoolpro.com">privacy@driveschoolpro.com</a>.</li>
</ul>

<p>The terms for using the pupil app are in our <a href="/pupil-terms/">Pupil Terms</a>.</p>

<h2 id="ai">6. AI features</h2>

<p>DriveSchoolPro uses an AI model (Claude, made by Anthropic) to write:</p>
<ul>
<li>a short <strong>briefing</strong> for the instructor before a lesson;</li>
<li>short <strong>lesson and pupil summaries</strong> for the instructor;</li>
<li>draft replies to <strong>support requests</strong>, and wording for some of our <strong>setup emails</strong>.</li>
</ul>

<p>What is sent for a briefing or summary: the pupil's <strong>first name only</strong>, the competencies practised and the level reached, the instructor's lesson outcome notes (up to three earlier lessons for a briefing) and the pupil learning notes the instructor wrote. <strong>The medical notes field is never sent.</strong> Free-text notes are sent as the instructor wrote them, so instructors are asked not to put health details in them.</p>

<p>The request goes through the Vercel AI Gateway to the Claude model, run by Anthropic in the US. If Anthropic is unavailable, the gateway can send the request to the same Claude model run by Amazon Bedrock or Google Vertex AI. A person reviews every output: the briefing is advice to the instructor, not a decision about the pupil, and nothing decides anything about a pupil automatically.</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Training.</strong> We do not use your data to train AI models. Vercel states that its AI Gateway does not use prompts or responses for training and does not keep them.</li>
<li><strong>Retention.</strong> Anthropic states that by default it deletes API inputs and outputs within 30 days.</li>
<li><strong>Switching it off.</strong> There is no setting to turn AI briefings off for a school or a pupil. The briefing job runs for every school. A school that objects should email <a href="mailto:privacy@driveschoolpro.com">privacy@driveschoolpro.com</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="messages">7. Text messages, WhatsApp and email</h2>

<ul>
<li><strong>Email.</strong> Lesson reminders, receipts and account notices go out through Resend. Pupils and parents have preferences for reminders, lesson emails and marketing, and every marketing email has an unsubscribe link.</li>
<li><strong>Text messages to pupils.</strong> Text reminders to pupils are not available in DriveSchoolPro today.</li>
<li><strong>WhatsApp.</strong> WhatsApp reminders are not yet offered to schools. Our <a href="/whatsapp/">WhatsApp policy</a> explains how opt-in works. Where a pupil opts in to WhatsApp messages, their mobile number is used only to send transactional messages about their lessons, and they can reply STOP at any time. We do not share, sell or rent mobile numbers or messaging opt-in consent to any third party for its own marketing.</li>
<li><strong>Texts to school owners.</strong> If you give a UK mobile number while setting up your school, we may send up to two texts about finishing setup, from a DriveSchoolPro number, via Twilio. Reply STOP to stop them. We keep a record that you opted out.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="sharing">8. Who we share data with</h2>

<p>We share personal data with service providers who process it for us under their written terms. Each one is listed with its purpose, location and transfer protection on our <a href="/subprocessors/">sub-processors page</a>. In summary:</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Hosting, database and file storage:</strong> Vercel, Neon, Amazon Web Services (backups).</li>
<li><strong>Payments:</strong> Stripe.</li>
<li><strong>Email, push and text messages:</strong> Resend, Google Firebase, Twilio.</li>
<li><strong>AI:</strong> Anthropic, through Vercel (and, if Anthropic is unavailable, the same model run by Amazon Bedrock or Google Vertex AI).</li>
<li><strong>Errors, analytics and security:</strong> Sentry, PostHog, Upstash.</li>
<li><strong>Support and internal alerts:</strong> Freshworks (Freshdesk), Slack.</li>
<li><strong>Maps, addresses and car pictures:</strong> Google Maps, Imagin Studio.</li>
<li><strong>Marketing:</strong> Mailchimp (account owners who opted in), Google Analytics and Google Ads, Metricool (website only, with consent).</li>
<li><strong>This website:</strong> Amazon Web Services (hosting), Formspree (contact form), Google Fonts, Arcade (product demos).</li>
</ul>

<p>A pupil's data is also visible to their own school and instructors. If a school connects its own Stripe account, Stripe is also in a direct relationship with that school and with the person paying.</p>

<p>We may share data where the law requires, with a regulator or the police, or to protect people. We do not sell personal data.</p>

<h2 id="cookies">9. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>

<p><strong>Strictly necessary</strong> (always on): a sign-in cookie, security tokens, and a record of your cookie choice. They are needed to run the service.</p>

<p>This website and the DriveSchoolPro app (app.driveschoolpro.com) each ask for your cookie choice and remember it separately. Answering the banner on one does not answer it on the other. On this website your choice is kept in your browser's storage and in a cookie called <code>dsp_consent</code> for up to 12 months; the app keeps its own record in your browser's storage.</p>

<p><strong>Optional</strong> (only after you click <strong>Accept All</strong>):</p>
<ul>
<li>Google Analytics and Google Ads on our website, to measure how visitors use it and which adverts led to a sign-up, and to show our adverts to past visitors;</li>
<li>Metricool, a website statistics tag;</li>
<li>in the app, PostHog product analytics and screen recordings of <strong>school-side</strong> screens, with on-screen text masked (apart from parts of our own screens we have marked as holding no personal data) and everything you type hidden, never on pupil or parent pages;</li>
<li>in the app, Google Analytics, if it is switched on. Unlike PostHog, it is not limited to school-side screens: after "Accept All" it loads on every page of the app, including pupil and parent pages.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Without cookies</strong> (whatever you choose): Vercel counts page visits and page speed without cookies; our servers send a few account-level usage events to PostHog (see below); Sentry records errors, and masked recordings of a sample of sessions (about one in ten, and every session with an error). Sentry's recordings are not tied to your choice in the cookie banner.</p>

<p>When you click through to sign up, the link to app.driveschoolpro.com can carry the campaign details from the page you landed on (for example which advert or website sent you). This is passed in the web address, not stored on your device, and is saved with your account so we know which marketing works.</p>

<h3>Product usage events sent from our servers</h3>
<p>To understand how schools use DriveSchoolPro and to improve it, our servers send a small number of account-level usage events to PostHog, which stores them in the EU. The events record steps such as signing up, adding a first pupil, booking a first lesson, finishing setup, starting a subscription and importing pupils (the number imported only). Each event is linked to your school's account by an internal school ID, not by your name or email address, and includes your plan, the number of days since you signed up, and a short tag for how you found us. The events contain no names, email addresses, phone numbers or pupil details. They use no cookies and store nothing on your device. Lawful basis: legitimate interests. To object, email <a href="mailto:privacy@driveschoolpro.com">privacy@driveschoolpro.com</a> and we will stop sending these events for your school.</p>

<h3>Changing your choice</h3>
<p>On this website, use <strong>Cookie settings</strong> at the foot of any page, or the button below, to see the banner again and choose again. In the app, clear the stored data for app.driveschoolpro.com in your browser settings and the app's banner will ask again.</p>

<p>
  <button
    type="button"
    data-cookie-settings
    class="text-sm px-4 py-2 rounded-lg border border-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors cursor-pointer"
  >
    Cookie settings
  </button>
</p>

<p>You can also install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.</p>

<h2 id="retention">10. How long we keep data</h2>

<p>As controller:</p>

<div class="overflow-x-auto">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>How long</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Account details of an active account</td><td>While the account is open</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Closed accounts</td><td>Kept 30 days after you ask to close, so you can export or change your mind. Then personal details are replaced with placeholders. Financial records stay for 6 years (HMRC)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Financial and audit records</td><td>6 years</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Records of completed erasure requests</td><td>6 years</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Email, text and WhatsApp delivery logs</td><td>90 days</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Setup and webhook queues</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Read in-app notifications</td><td>180 days</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Message content in the communication log</td><td>Anonymised after 2 years</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Marketing list</td><td>Until you unsubscribe, then removed</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Backups</td><td>Daily copies for 30 days; one copy a month for 12 months. Copies expire on that cycle, so a deleted record can stay in a backup until then</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<p>Our analytics, error-reporting and contact-form providers (PostHog, Sentry and Formspree) keep data for the periods set in those services. Ask <a href="mailto:privacy@driveschoolpro.com">privacy@driveschoolpro.com</a> if you want to know a current period.</p>

<p>As processor, we keep pupil data for as long as the school's account is open and then as the <a href="/data-processing-terms/">Data Processing Terms</a> say. Uploaded document files are not removed from storage automatically when an account is erased today; we delete them by hand within 30 days of a written request.</p>

<h2 id="your-rights">11. Your rights, and how to use them</h2>

<p>You can ask us to: give you a copy of your data; correct it; erase it; restrict its use; give it to you in a portable form; or stop using it where we rely on legitimate interests. Where we rely on consent, you can withdraw it at any time. Withdrawing does not affect what we did before.</p>

<p><strong>If we are the controller</strong>, email <a href="mailto:privacy@driveschoolpro.com">privacy@driveschoolpro.com</a>. We aim to reply within one month. We may ask you to prove who you are.</p>

<p><strong>If your data is a pupil record,</strong> the school or instructor decides. Email them, or email us and we will pass it on within 5 working days and help them answer within the month. An account owner can export the whole school's data from Settings &gt; Profile in the app, and a pupil who uses the pupil app can download their own data from their profile there. Archiving a pupil in the app hides the pupil but does not erase them. To erase one pupil completely, the school asks us at <a href="mailto:privacy@driveschoolpro.com">privacy@driveschoolpro.com</a>.</p>

<p>You can complain to us first, at <a href="mailto:privacy@driveschoolpro.com">privacy@driveschoolpro.com</a>, and we will acknowledge a complaint within 30 days. You can also complain to the <strong>Information Commissioner's Office</strong>: <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>, 0303 123 1113.</p>

<h2 id="transfers">12. Where your data goes</h2>

<p>Our app servers and main database are in London, and our database backups are in Ireland. Uploaded files are stored by Vercel. Some providers are US companies. Where data goes outside the UK, we rely on UK adequacy regulations, the UK Extension to the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, or the UK International Data Transfer Addendum or Agreement in the provider's terms. The <a href="/subprocessors/">sub-processors page</a> shows what each provider's own terms say. Ask for details at <a href="mailto:privacy@driveschoolpro.com">privacy@driveschoolpro.com</a>.</p>

<h2 id="security">13. Security</h2>

<p>Encryption in transit (HTTPS) and at rest in the database; passwords stored as bcrypt hashes; school accounts kept separate by organisation checks in our code; role-based access; login throttling; an audit log; nightly encrypted backups with a weekly test restore. No system is perfectly secure. If a breach affects pupil data, we tell the school, as our <a href="/data-processing-terms/">Data Processing Terms</a> set out. Where we are the controller, we tell you and the ICO as the law requires.</p>

<h2 id="changes">14. Changes to this notice</h2>

<p>If we make a material change, we update the date above, and email account owners at least 30 days ahead for anything that affects them.</p>

